 "source_url": "https://www.livingstone.qld.gov.au/files/sharedassets/public/v/1/doing-business/documents/Schedules.pdf",
 "purpose": "Councils own fact sheet (https://www.livingstone.qld.gov.au/downloads/file/173/heritage-places, link now broken) states the current Livingstone Shire Council Local Heritage Register (2018 scheme, overlay code 8.2.9) was derived from the 103 listings in this 2005-scheme Schedule 3. The 2018 scheme's own Heritage Place Overlay Code (08_Pt8_829) and Schedule 2 mapping index do not repeat this list as text - the only place the current local register's membership exists publicly is the council's OM25 map layer, which is ArcGIS TilesOnly (not queryable). This file is the best available text substitute: the 2005 predecessor list, by name/property description/locality, matched here against the current state cadastre.",
 "extraction_method": "Schedules.pdf table text extracted word-by-word (PyMuPDF get_text('words')) and reconstructed into the table's 4 columns (Cultural feature / Property description or location / Reason for listing / Locality) by X-position bucketing, then rows assembled by Y-range overlap across columns (not naive index-pairing, which was tried first and found to drift - e.g. it mismatched 'Sambo's house site' to the wrong lot; verified correct by direct visual inspection of the rendered PDF page against the Y-overlap reconstruction, 3 Nov 2026). 104 records recovered.",
 "cadastre_match_method": "Property description parsed for a 'Lot N [and M] [Plan] XXnnnnn' pattern, then queried against the state cadastre (spatial-gis.information.qld.gov.au/.../PlanningCadastre/LandParcelPropertyFramework/MapServer/4, field lotplan) on 3 Nov 2026. 86 of 104 records had a parseable lot/plan; 67 of those 86 still resolve to a real, current parcel. The other 19 no longer resolve by that lot/plan - likely renumbered/resurveyed in the ~20 years since 2005 (same pattern found for Burke Shire's Schedule 5, where 5 of 9 also failed to resolve). The remaining 18 records give only a road/description location (e.g. 'Joskeleigh Road, Joskeleigh'), never a lot/plan, and cannot be matched to a parcel at all.",
 "caveat": "A resolved match is reliable (a real, current parcel at that lot/plan). An unresolved one is NOT conclusive evidence the place no longer exists or isn't on the current register - it only means this specific 2005-era lot/plan reference doesn't resolve today. Also: this 2005 list may not be identical to the 2018 register (places may have been added or removed when the register was carried over) - treat a hit as 'historically a locally significant place here, confirm against Council's current register', not as a definitive current-register citation.",
